  "placement": "Book page 38, topic 2.3: স্কেলার ও ভেক্টর রাশি. Next to চিত্র ২.০৩ (vectors A, B, C, D), or in place of it.",
  "order": 1,
  "maintainers": ["RadeenXALNW"],
  "units": "mm",
  "description": "Interactive 3D version of the book's চিত্র ২.০৩ (page 38, 2.3): four arrow pieces A, B, C, D lie on graph paper with a compass rose, beside a thermometer reading 37° C. Drag an arrow by its body to move it (its মান and দিক stay the same: the same vector), drag its head to turn it to another compass direction (দিক) or stretch it (মান, counted by the marks on it, one per unit); the panel says what changed. Drop an arrow on another's tail to compare: only when মান and দিক are both equal are they the same vector, wherever they were drawn; both দিক arcs are drawn and the caption's verdicts are given in the book's words. Move or turn the thermometer and nothing changes: a temperature has a মান and no দিক (a scalar). Buttons line up the book's pairs A–B, A–C, C–D. Test tab: 5 questions (which arrow equals A, why two vectors differ, scalar, vector or not a quantity (or the hand-written notation), what makes '4 km from home' a position, reading an arrow's মান and দিক). Phone-first, Bangla.",
  "tags": ["vector", "scalar", "magnitude", "direction", "temperature", "motion", "bangla"],
